I want to support the content below as a command line app called bfr. 
I want it to be in Typescript, driven by yargs, and have it maintain its context/state
via an app configuration directory on the user's directory path in a directory named .bfr -
the goal is contexts can be established on the command line and maintained in this directory
for later reference and access.

# This comment section describes some of how the app should work
# context concept is equivalent of environment variables, but established so that cmd line app can 
# maintain its own context variables and settings given a "context-id"? 
# "context-key" establishes proof of context authority (e.g. permission to delete/update?)
# "context-ttl" gives a maximum amount of time-to-live for default context to be settable 
#    (e.g. can't be updated after this time-to-live has expired)
# Here's an example which clears the previous context, sets a new one and establishes it for
# following commands to execute against, then creates users and chat room.

bfr unset-default-context [context-id]
bfr set-default-context [context-id] [context-key] [context-ttl]

bfr set-context CHAT_NAME "My Fun Chat"
bfr set-context HOST_USER_ID user1
bfr set-context USER2_ID user2
bfr set-context USER3_ID user3


bfr add-user user1
bfr add-user user2


bfr create-chat *CHAT_NAME* --host *HOST_USER_ID*
bfr update-chat-users *USER2_ID* *USER3_ID*
bfr start-chat-room


bfr unset-default-context
